prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids has a record from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 181% of normal in April to May and 32% in July to August. Every one of the 7 grids had its driest year in 1963, with grid 18762 at 60%. In 2026 so far the middle published 45% for January to February, and grid 19063 has a preliminary estimate of 41.4 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
